.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt TUNEFS_EXT2FS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tunefs_ext2fs
.Nd change parameters of an existing ext2 file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl C Ar mount-count
.Op Fl c Ar max-mount-count
.Op Fl e Cm continue | remount-ro | panic
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl g Ar group
.Op Fl i Ar interval
.Op Fl j
.Op Fl J Ar size=journal-size
.Op Fl L Ar volume-label
.Op Fl M Ar last-mounted-directory
.Op Fl m Ar reserved-percent
.Op Fl O Ar feature Ns Op , Ns Ar ...
.Op Fl p
.Op Fl r Ar reserved-blocks
.Op Fl T Ar last-check-time
.Op Fl U Ar uuid
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Ar filesys | device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility changes parameters of an existing ext2, ext3, or ext4 file system.
It is the ext2 counterpart of
.Xr tunefs 8 .
The file system must not be mounted.
.Pp
The parameters which are to be changed are indicated by the flags
given below:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl C Ar mount-count
Set the number of times the file system has been mounted.
.It Fl c Ar max-mount-count
Set the number of mounts after which the file system is checked by
.Xr fsck_ext2fs 8 .
A value of 0 disables mount-count checking.
.It Fl e Cm continue | remount-ro | panic
Set the behavior when an error is detected:
.Cm continue
continues normally,
.Cm remount-ro
remounts the file system read-only, and
.Cm panic
causes a kernel panic.
.It Fl f
Force the operation even when the file system is marked unclean or needs
journal recovery.
The file system must still be unmounted.
.It Fl g Ar group
Set the group allowed to use the reserved blocks.
The argument may be a group name or a numeric group ID.
.It Fl i Ar interval
Set the interval between file system checks.
The interval may be followed by
.Cm d ,
.Cm m ,
or
.Cm w
to select days, months, or weeks.
A value of 0 disables interval checking.
.It Fl j
Add an internal journal to an ext4 file system.
Journal creation requires the
.Dq extent
feature; plain ext2 and ext3 file systems are not supported.
The default journal size is 1024 file system blocks.
.It Fl J Ar size=journal-size
Set the journal size in megabytes and add a journal, as with
.Fl j .
This option currently accepts only the
.Cm size=
parameter.
.It Fl L Ar volume-label
Set the volume label.
The label may be at most 15 characters drawn from letters, digits,
.Sy _
and
.Sy - .
.It Fl M Ar last-mounted-directory
Set the directory on which the file system was last mounted.
.It Fl m Ar reserved-percent
Set the percentage of blocks reserved for the super-user.
The value must be between 0 and 99.
.It Fl O Ar feature Ns Op , Ns Ar ...
Set or clear file system features.
Prefix a feature with
.Sy ^
to clear it.
The supported features are
.Cm dir_index ,
.Cm dir_nlink ,
.Cm extra_isize ,
.Cm filetype ,
.Cm has_journal
(set only, equivalent to
.Fl j ) ,
.Cm huge_file ,
.Cm large_file ,
.Cm metadata_csum_seed ,
.Cm read-only ,
.Cm resize_inode
(clear only), and
.Cm sparse_super
(set only).
Structural features such as
.Cm 64bit ,
.Cm extent ,
.Cm flex_bg ,
.Cm metadata_csum ,
.Cm mmp ,
.Cm project ,
.Cm quota ,
and
.Cm uninit_bg
are not supported.
After changing
.Cm dir_index ,
.Cm filetype ,
.Cm resize_inode ,
or
.Cm sparse_super ,
run
.Xr fsck_ext2fs 8
to repair dependent metadata.
.It Fl p
Print the current parameters and exit without changing the file system.
.It Fl r Ar reserved-blocks
Set the number of blocks reserved for the super-user.
This takes precedence over
.Fl m .
.It Fl T Ar last-check-time
Set the time the file system was last checked.
The argument may be
.Cm now
or a date in the
.Dv YYYYMMDDHHMMSS
format.
.It Fl U Ar uuid
Set the universally unique identifier of the file system.
The argument may be a UUID,
.Cm clear ,
.Cm random ,
or
.Cm time .
On file systems with metadata checksums, the checksum seed is preserved.
.It Fl u Ar user
Set the user allowed to use the reserved blocks.
The argument may be a user name or a numeric user ID.
.El
.Pp
The primary superblock and all backup superblocks are updated.
The changes are written synchronously before
.Nm
exits.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ext2fs 4 ,
.Xr dumpfs_ext2fs 8 ,
.Xr fsck_ext2fs 8 ,
.Xr newfs_ext2fs 8 ,
.Xr tunefs 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility is currently under development and has not yet been released.
